#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059375 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "979859e4-b60c-548d-8da6-b180400e1b07" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Determinant of a 3x3 Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "14e05d4f-373c-5d1f-aa59-7ee52466480e" :question/math-academy-id "e-14762" :question/problem "Find the value of $\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 & 6 \\\\ 8 & 8 & 8 \\\\ -6 & -12 & 1\\end{aligned}$" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 & 6 \\\\ 8 & 8 & 8 \\\\ -6 & -12 & 1\\end{aligned}| & =0|\\begin{aligned}8 & 8 \\\\ -12 & 1\\end{aligned}|-(-3)|\\begin{aligned}8 & 8 \\\\ -6 & 1\\end{aligned}|+6|\\begin{aligned}8 & 8 \\\\ -6 & -12\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0(8+96)+3(8+48)+6(-96+48) \\\\  & =0+3\\cdot 56+6\\cdot (-48) \\\\  & =168-288 \\\\  & =-120\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059376 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "32df8909-a239-5167-b8ea-412f7cdaea93" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Singular Matrices"}] :question/id #uuid "d7516cec-bd96-59db-98cd-5d82e41fa719" :question/math-academy-id "e-14763" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $A$ given below?\n\n- $\\det(A) = 0$\n\n- $A$ is **not** a singular matrix\n\n- $A$ is a singular matrix\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 7\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that a square matrix is singular if its determinant is equal to $0.$\n\nUsing the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 7\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 7\\end{aligned}|-2|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 7\\end{aligned}|+3|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(0-4)-2(7-3)+3(4-0) \\\\  & =-4-2\\cdot 4+3\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =-4-8+12 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\det(A)=0$, the matrix is singular. \n\nTherefore, only statements I and III are true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059377 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ab642ad6-d9e0-5734-83b4-81627b9132eb" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for an Unknown Given the Determinant"}] :question/id #uuid "7780340c-43d6-5d38-9270-865914098218" :question/math-academy-id "e-14764" :question/problem "Given that the determinant of  $[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ k & 4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}]$ is $2,$ find the value of the constant $k.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $k\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ k & 4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}| & =3|\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}|-1|\\begin{aligned}k & 5 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}|+2|\\begin{aligned}k & 4 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3(12-10)-1(3k-0)+2(2k-0) \\\\  & =3\\cdot 2-1\\cdot 3k+2\\cdot 2k \\\\  & =6-3k+4k \\\\  & =k+6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the determinant of the matrix is $2,$ we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}k+6 & =2 \\\\ k & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303307 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "32df8909-a239-5167-b8ea-412f7cdaea93" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Singular Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8a191dba-16dd-5b91-b92c-74456c9286df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303309} {:answer/id #uuid "b5b00579-93ef-5741-b329-98cc98e20e8c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303310} {:answer/id #uuid "e0e1a3d4-3256-56a2-8579-d0cb7725057f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303311} {:answer/id #uuid "d91db950-9a7f-5572-9414-c66c3ae0f4a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303312} {:answer/id #uuid "8dac9c91-67ef-5130-939b-a0b625916607" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303313}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8a191dba-16dd-5b91-b92c-74456c9286df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303309} :answer-field/id #uuid "9d5536c7-7d93-5b6f-bcb0-08074eb5662e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303308}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1de7b7b6-d74a-53dc-9249-a5265a42e232" :question/math-academy-id "q-128476" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $T$ given below?\n\n- $T$ is a singular matrix\n- $T$ is **not** a singular matrix\n- $det(T)=-30$\n\n \n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -5 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that a square matrix is singular if its determinant is equal to $0.$\n\nUsing the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(T) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -5 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}|-3|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|-5|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(1-3)-3(2-1)-5(6-1) \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-2)-3\\cdot 1-5\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =-2-3-25 \\\\  & =-30\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince $det(T)=-30\\ne 0$, the matrix is **not** singular. \n\nTherefore, only statements II and III are true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186277588 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "32df8909-a239-5167-b8ea-412f7cdaea93" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Singular Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a7b52202-5838-5f29-a879-c2b165ec65a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277590} {:answer/id #uuid "2c96c50d-442d-5f35-9ce3-641ad01fa89d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277591} {:answer/id #uuid "d830578e-b1ce-5019-9827-ef1d027857fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277592} {:answer/id #uuid "31226bb1-7aa2-5b8d-b4d2-e4f06b081910" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277593} {:answer/id #uuid "934fefcf-c3c7-5069-a704-8f6172567660" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277594}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "31226bb1-7aa2-5b8d-b4d2-e4f06b081910" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277593} :answer-field/id #uuid "84cbf4eb-9c25-5589-8b2a-668a1583cc9e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277589}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "72bad0dd-a3a7-570e-b5f6-c6a202014e4a" :question/math-academy-id "q-128484" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $R$ given below?\n\n- $R$ is a singular matrix\n- $det(R)=0$\n- $det(R)=1$\n\n \n\n$$\nR=[\\begin{aligned}2 & \\sqrt{2} & 2 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & \\sqrt{2} & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that a square matrix is singular if its determinant is equal to $0.$\n\nUsing the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(R) & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & \\sqrt{2} & 2 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & \\sqrt{2} & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2|\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ \\sqrt{2} & 4\\end{aligned}|-\\sqrt{2}|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} & -1 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}|+2|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} & 0 \\\\ 1 & \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2(0+\\sqrt{2})-\\sqrt{2}(2+1)+2(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}-0) \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\sqrt{2}-\\sqrt{2}\\cdot 3+2\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}-3\\sqrt{2}+\\sqrt{2} \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince $det(R)=0$, the matrix is singular. \n\nTherefore, only statements I and II are true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186291607 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ab642ad6-d9e0-5734-83b4-81627b9132eb" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for an Unknown Given the Determinant"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d0cb28e-4fc8-5013-94cf-ff5147e66641" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-2$ and $3$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291609} {:answer/id #uuid "31ed3d39-28ce-5447-8827-dde43b2a8108" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$5$ and $6$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291610} {:answer/id #uuid "d58f196e-d677-589c-a2c1-6f3365a23a8d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$6$ and $7$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291611} {:answer/id #uuid "81cfc9c1-3416-5a42-8690-032d7c913f56" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$3$  only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291612} {:answer/id #uuid "5b771a52-6452-59ae-8bf1-004cc6984d54" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$5$ and $-5$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291613}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d58f196e-d677-589c-a2c1-6f3365a23a8d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$6$ and $7$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291611} :answer-field/id #uuid "0e5f0f38-246f-5927-9460-4b2aff199937" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291608}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d07c9ad8-9277-516a-802b-f65168b9d077" :question/math-academy-id "q-130575" :question/problem "Given that the determinant of\n$[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 3 & z \\\\ z & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]$\nis $-48$, find all the possible values of $z.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 3 & z \\\\ z & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}| & =2|\\begin{aligned}3 & z \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}|-1|\\begin{aligned}2 & z \\\\ z & 1\\end{aligned}|+5|\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ z & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2(3+z)-(2-{z}^{2})+5(-2-3z) \\\\  & =6+2z-2+{z}^{2}-10-15z \\\\  & ={z}^{2}-13z-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the determinant of the matrix is $-48,$ we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}^{2}-13z-6 & =-48 \\\\ {z}^{2}-13z+42 & =0 \\\\ z & =\\frac{-(-13)\\pm \\sqrt{{13}^{2}-4\\cdot 1\\cdot 42}}{2\\cdot 1} \\\\  & =\\frac{13\\pm \\sqrt{1}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{13\\pm 1}{2} \\\\  & =6,7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $z=6$ and $z=7.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303314 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ab642ad6-d9e0-5734-83b4-81627b9132eb" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for an Unknown Given the Determinant"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c19ee59f-4480-595d-be78-0612dc30906d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303316} {:answer/id #uuid "e68058e1-4682-5ab8-b703-62cc2f118682" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303317} {:answer/id #uuid "8e5485a5-a0ae-50cc-8dbe-9aab77f55a9b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303318} {:answer/id #uuid "d6bee06f-bbf2-5d38-83f4-80d000dc236e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303319} {:answer/id #uuid "45831162-173d-54b1-b3e2-550e320a21bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303320}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "45831162-173d-54b1-b3e2-550e320a21bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303320} :answer-field/id #uuid "abfe5887-0d05-5018-9ee0-2ab1a972fca7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303315}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "799ed291-cfbc-56bf-891a-7ba1b277d3e5" :question/math-academy-id "q-18252" :question/problem "Find the possible values of the constant $p$ given that the matrix $[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 6 & -5 & 2p-4\\end{aligned}]$ is singular." :question/worked-solution "First, let's use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 6 & -5 & 2p-4\\end{aligned}| & =1|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -5 & 2p-4\\end{aligned}|-0|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 6 & 2p-4\\end{aligned}|+1|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 6 & -5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(2p-4+10)-0+(-10-6) \\\\  & =2p-4+10-10-6 \\\\  & =2p-10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the matrix is singular, the determinant is $0.$ So,  we have:\n\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2p-10 & =0 \\\\ 2p & =10 \\\\ p & =\\frac{10}{2} \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $p=5.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303321 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ab642ad6-d9e0-5734-83b4-81627b9132eb" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for an Unknown Given the Determinant"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20471aec-848e-513e-968a-d6aec97caa96" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-\\frac{25}{9}$ and $1$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303323} {:answer/id #uuid "b476adf8-40ae-54da-ac98-df291a8dd1ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-\\frac{5}{3}$ and $1$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303324} {:answer/id #uuid "09c5767d-a3b0-5d1a-860a-026fafd6510c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-1$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303325} {:answer/id #uuid "f5001a26-00b9-5b68-b868-a2749147bd0f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-\\frac{5}{3}$ and $-1$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303326} {:answer/id #uuid "e19af8f1-f3a5-5db5-ac86-072cb48385c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-\\frac{25}{9}$ and $-1$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303327}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e19af8f1-f3a5-5db5-ac86-072cb48385c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-\\frac{25}{9}$ and $-1$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303327} :answer-field/id #uuid "59e39d2d-4575-5e43-a400-caa5668def86" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303322}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "01aa8d57-113b-5436-b1ef-e962e4723b9f" :question/math-academy-id "q-18256" :question/problem "Given that the determinant of \n$[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -3y & -2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & y & -5\\end{aligned}]$\n is $81,$ find all the possible values of $y.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -3y & -2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & y & -5\\end{aligned}| & =4|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ y & -5\\end{aligned}|-2|\\begin{aligned}-3y & 1 \\\\ 2 & -5\\end{aligned}|+3|\\begin{aligned}-3y & -2 \\\\ 2 & y\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4\\cdot (10-y)-2\\cdot (15y-2)+3\\cdot (-3{y}^{2}+4) \\\\  & =40-4y-30y+4-9{y}^{2}+12 \\\\  & =-9{y}^{2}-34y+56\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the determinant of the matrix is $81,$ we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-9{y}^{2}-34y+56 & =81 \\\\ -9{y}^{2}-34y-25 & =0 \\\\ 9{y}^{2}+34y+25 & =0 \\\\ y & =\\frac{-34\\pm \\sqrt{{34}^{2}-4\\cdot 9\\cdot 25}}{2\\cdot 9} \\\\  & =\\frac{-34\\pm \\sqrt{256}}{18} \\\\  & =\\frac{-34\\pm 16}{18} \\\\  & =\\frac{-17\\pm 8}{9}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $y=-\\frac{25}{9}$ and $y=-1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303328 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ab642ad6-d9e0-5734-83b4-81627b9132eb" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for an Unknown Given the Determinant"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b3d28b60-d649-5c6d-8573-0304c956c863" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303330} {:answer/id #uuid "9fcad194-d0fc-5eab-847b-e2ee02f0d1dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2$ and $4$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303331} {:answer/id #uuid "9caf0e2d-0e52-528d-9644-e1afdc7bc6e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-2$ and $5$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303332} {:answer/id #uuid "6cf0f426-12d6-5ead-9702-991f8e82b826" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$5$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303333} {:answer/id #uuid "6aeafd29-6f04-5efa-b049-57d00d3068b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4$ and $5$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303334}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9caf0e2d-0e52-528d-9644-e1afdc7bc6e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-2$ and $5$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303332} :answer-field/id #uuid "47ef13ae-3048-55d4-a544-a1da4c5bbca1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303329}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "408197de-567d-5d88-85f3-7d29be5c6d83" :question/math-academy-id "q-18272" :question/problem "Given that $M=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & p & 0 \\\\ p-3 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]$ and $det(M)=-23,$ find all the possible values of $p.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(M) & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & p & 0 \\\\ p-3 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0|\\begin{aligned}p & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}|-(-3)|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ p-3 & -1\\end{aligned}|+2|\\begin{aligned}1 & p \\\\ p-3 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0+3\\cdot (-1)+2\\cdot (3p-{p}^{2}) \\\\  & =-3-2{p}^{2}+6p \\\\  & =-2{p}^{2}+6p-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the determinant of the matrix is $-23,$ we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2{p}^{2}+6p-3 & =-23 \\\\ 2{p}^{2}-6p-20 & =0 \\\\ {p}^{2}-3p-10 & =0 \\\\ p & =\\frac{-(-3)\\pm \\sqrt{(-3)^{2}-4\\cdot 1\\cdot (-10)}}{2\\cdot 1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\pm \\sqrt{49}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\pm 7}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,  the solutions are $p=-2$ and $p=5.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303335 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "979859e4-b60c-548d-8da6-b180400e1b07" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Determinant of a 3x3 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08ccffa7-0e8b-5570-b754-d53696a9cabf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "64" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303337}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "08ccffa7-0e8b-5570-b754-d53696a9cabf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "64" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303337} :answer-field/id #uuid "7bc89ee6-7b05-53be-a8d5-23856f8b47c3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303336}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "14ff8d5f-11fc-5853-ae2e-523aaa9718fa" :question/math-academy-id "q-275585" :question/problem "If $A=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 7 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -3\\end{aligned}],$ then $det(A)=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Using the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}-5 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 7 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -3\\end{aligned}| & =-5|\\begin{aligned}7 & 5 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{aligned}|-3|\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}|+0|\\begin{aligned}1 & 7 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-5(-21-(-10))-3(-3-0)+0 \\\\  & =-5\\cdot (-11)-3\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =55+9 \\\\  & =64\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186277616 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "979859e4-b60c-548d-8da6-b180400e1b07" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Determinant of a 3x3 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7e23f9df-fd1c-5fb0-94ae-f6375cd3d955" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-146" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277618} {:answer/id #uuid "c22de81e-b56f-5bb2-89dd-beb6da000fae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "146" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303338}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7e23f9df-fd1c-5fb0-94ae-f6375cd3d955" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-146" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277618} :answer-field/id #uuid "ab1047e4-3763-5e81-9313-32ad69e87013" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277617}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ab606913-f467-54bc-b8f4-c2c664d43234" :question/math-academy-id "q-280387" :question/problem "If $H=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 7 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -5 \\\\ 4 & -3 & 0\\end{aligned}],$ then $det(H)=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Using the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}0 & 7 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -5 \\\\ 4 & -3 & 0\\end{aligned}| & =0|\\begin{aligned}0 & -5 \\\\ -3 & 0\\end{aligned}|-7|\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{aligned}|+2|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0-7(0-(-20))+2(-3-0) \\\\  & =-7\\cdot (20)+2\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =-140-6 \\\\  & =-146\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303339 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "979859e4-b60c-548d-8da6-b180400e1b07" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Determinant of a 3x3 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8ff34e01-249d-5f34-a6ee-d7b6e18a50c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303341} {:answer/id #uuid "d14d2afd-862f-529e-bfcf-55965bdfb7a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303342}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d14d2afd-862f-529e-bfcf-55965bdfb7a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303342} :answer-field/id #uuid "18824b8b-d559-5060-91df-b38c33b99b4d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303340}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "711f7b0f-8038-59ce-9d0e-6b423dd7512d" :question/math-academy-id "q-280390" :question/problem "If $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}],$ then $det(A)=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Using the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}| & =0|\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}|-2|\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}|+(-3)|\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0-2(0-0)-3(0-0) \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186277622 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "979859e4-b60c-548d-8da6-b180400e1b07" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Determinant of a 3x3 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cc5a18cf-619b-5487-8d6e-7bb9706e4c13" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-33" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277624}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cc5a18cf-619b-5487-8d6e-7bb9706e4c13" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-33" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277624} :answer-field/id #uuid "5aa8dc84-e4fd-5d51-b298-97c10fc7b514" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277623}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e83248f9-81a1-5e37-b8ca-6d95511aa92e" :question/math-academy-id "q-280394" :question/problem "If $R=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 6 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}],$ then $det(R)=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Using the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 6 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}| & =1|\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|-(-2)|\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 \\\\ 6 & 2\\end{aligned}|+0|\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ 6 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(3\\cdot 2-5\\cdot (-1))+2(4\\cdot 2-5\\cdot 6)+0 \\\\  & =1(6+5)+2(8-30) \\\\  & =11+2(-22) \\\\  & =11-44 \\\\  & =-33\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303343 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "979859e4-b60c-548d-8da6-b180400e1b07" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Determinant of a 3x3 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a865554-0a16-5080-a9ac-454763f1b02a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303345} {:answer/id #uuid "70a3288c-9a8b-5258-a31a-e86f7929ead4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303346} {:answer/id #uuid "3cf721f7-87c3-51fa-aaf3-91839fc65583" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303347} {:answer/id #uuid "31b4cba5-feaf-5b8a-a451-d244cad17919" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303348} {:answer/id #uuid "5edc7390-a20c-5673-9b84-c60171d426fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303349}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3cf721f7-87c3-51fa-aaf3-91839fc65583" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303347} :answer-field/id #uuid "216ec6d2-dd2c-5323-ac0f-4bb01f046b29" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303344}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4620a567-cdc4-53d7-9a4f-ea734b82495f" :question/math-academy-id "q-38100" :question/problem "Find the value of $|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 8\\end{aligned}|.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 8\\end{aligned}| & =1|\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 8\\end{aligned}|-(-1)|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 8\\end{aligned}|+2|\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(32-0)+1(0-0)+2(0-0) \\\\  & =1\\cdot 32 \\\\  & =32\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186280906 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "32df8909-a239-5167-b8ea-412f7cdaea93" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Singular Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bb4ba432-2a8f-5769-8c7b-3bf2be07a4ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280908} {:answer/id #uuid "40bf93a9-0e1a-5d27-a8f0-f3f34430aa2c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280909} {:answer/id #uuid "1453c279-fab3-529d-aaba-4443449a3b23" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280910} {:answer/id #uuid "a0810cfc-2716-503e-8eda-9bd7b08acab6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280911} {:answer/id #uuid "ce492c35-85b8-5d30-8cc7-1882be5a74c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280912}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ce492c35-85b8-5d30-8cc7-1882be5a74c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280912} :answer-field/id #uuid "84ed8533-f1fb-5df4-95a9-e6288fd5e96f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280907}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4646eada-04b7-5167-b329-286673c2150b" :question/math-academy-id "q-38182" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $Q$ given below?\n\n- $Q$ is **not** a singular matrix\n- $Q$ is a singular matrix\n- $det(Q)=-5$\n\n$$\nQ=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 7 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 8\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that a square matrix is singular if its determinant is equal to $0.$\n\nUsing the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(Q) & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 7 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 8\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0|\\begin{aligned}4 & 7 \\\\ 5 & 8\\end{aligned}|-3|\\begin{aligned}1 & 7 \\\\ 2 & 8\\end{aligned}|+6|\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0-3(8-14)+6(5-8) \\\\  & =0-3\\cdot (-6)+6\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =18-18 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(Q)=0$, the matrix is singular. \n\nTherefore, only statement II is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303350 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "32df8909-a239-5167-b8ea-412f7cdaea93" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Singular Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9def4b4a-1dd6-546f-a05a-5cec780136ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I  only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303352} {:answer/id #uuid "ea8d1bfd-dd9d-5df0-bb07-aecfb19ecda9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303353} {:answer/id #uuid "e3c5ada5-b582-58a4-9b16-63c359d07add" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III  only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303354} {:answer/id #uuid "19695a11-6184-50a6-b7e4-a8ce98068372" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303355} {:answer/id #uuid "7e56084e-c049-5d03-8053-7d8f8a131ad4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303356}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9def4b4a-1dd6-546f-a05a-5cec780136ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I  only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303352} :answer-field/id #uuid "e5ffcb6e-0917-5f6f-a0aa-f5850879ca37" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303351}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f488e99f-6a91-5199-9a3f-4686ca4250e2" :question/math-academy-id "q-77477" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $S$ given below?\n\n- $S$ is **not** a singular matrix\n- $S$ is a singular matrix\n- $det(S)=\\sqrt{3}$\n\n$$\nS=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & \\,0 \\\\ 2 & \\sqrt{3} & \\,\\,-1 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 4 & \\,\\,-\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that a square matrix is singular if its determinant is equal to $0.$\n\nUsing the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(S) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & \\,0 \\\\ 2 & \\sqrt{3} & \\,\\,-1 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 4 & \\,\\,-\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1|\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3} & \\,\\,-1 \\\\ 4 & \\,\\,-\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}|-2|\\begin{aligned}2 & \\,-1 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & \\,-\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}|+0|\\begin{aligned}2 & \\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(-{(\\sqrt{3})}^{2}+4)-2(-2\\sqrt{3}+\\sqrt{3})+0 \\\\  & =(-3+4)-2\\cdot (-\\sqrt{3}) \\\\  & =1+2\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(S)=1+2\\sqrt{3}\\ne 0$, the matrix is **not ** singular. \n\nTherefore, only statement I is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303357 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "32df8909-a239-5167-b8ea-412f7cdaea93" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Singular Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b9405d7f-2eab-599d-9ba5-e87cacabdf95" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303359} {:answer/id #uuid "8b70e71f-f769-57db-b7fb-a5767752d8e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303360} {:answer/id #uuid "916c7451-7165-5939-b18f-f24a87f57db6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303361} {:answer/id #uuid "8e92102a-d2be-58f6-bc96-f9d23e118a46" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303362} {:answer/id #uuid "341dcfd3-2a7a-54a5-a51a-2cd79256e8e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303363}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "341dcfd3-2a7a-54a5-a51a-2cd79256e8e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303363} :answer-field/id #uuid "92720cbe-efa5-5123-a597-8ee071c3b10d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303358}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "24cc52a8-4124-5277-acdf-def6004941a2" :question/math-academy-id "q-77478" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $R$ given below?\n\n- $R$ is a singular matrix\n- $det(R)=0$\n- $det(R)=1$\n\n \n\n$$\nR=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{5} & \\frac{2}{5} & \\frac{1}{5} \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{2} & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that a square matrix is singular if its determinant is equal to $0.$\n\nUsing the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(R) & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{5} & \\frac{2}{5} & \\frac{1}{5} \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{2} & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5}|\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & 1\\end{aligned}|-\\frac{2}{5}|\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|+\\frac{1}{5}|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5}(2-\\frac{3}{2})-\\frac{2}{5}(1-0)+\\frac{1}{5}(\\frac{1}{2}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{2}{5}\\cdot 1+\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{10}-\\frac{2}{5}+\\frac{1}{10} \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince $det(R)=0$, the matrix is singular. \n\nTherefore, only statements I and II are true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303364 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ab642ad6-d9e0-5734-83b4-81627b9132eb" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for an Unknown Given the Determinant"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a9f6f207-5255-5a28-a04e-80e38de92f2d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-3$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303366} {:answer/id #uuid "2be20272-a5bf-59ff-9941-778dee46a8a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$0$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303367} {:answer/id #uuid "bf3791e4-4ff9-5228-b34d-8c28ddd53705" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$0$ and $-3$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303368} {:answer/id #uuid "1e2b4530-3acf-5293-ad27-be2c0e8f23dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$3$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303369} {:answer/id #uuid "541648f0-0186-5eeb-a1cc-3f78dbdc070b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$0$ and $3$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303370}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "541648f0-0186-5eeb-a1cc-3f78dbdc070b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$0$ and $3$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303370} :answer-field/id #uuid "39ec0585-2cae-5922-9587-17c41dd6003c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303365}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b27fea7a-77af-5ede-b5e2-28d0928e1d9b" :question/math-academy-id "q-9911" :question/problem "Find the possible values of the constant $k$ given that the matrix\n$[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & k \\\\ 1 & k & -k \\\\ 5 & k & k\\end{aligned}]$ is singular." :question/worked-solution "First, let's use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & k \\\\ 1 & k & -k \\\\ 5 & k & k\\end{aligned}| & =1|\\begin{aligned}k & -k \\\\ k & k\\end{aligned}|-(-1)|\\begin{aligned}1 & -k \\\\ 5 & k\\end{aligned}|+k|\\begin{aligned}1 & k \\\\ 5 & k\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =({k}^{2}+{k}^{2})+(k+5k)+k(k-5k) \\\\  & =2{k}^{2}+6k+k\\cdot (-4k) \\\\  & =2{k}^{2}+6k-4{k}^{2} \\\\  & =-2{k}^{2}+6k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the matrix is singular, the determinant is $0,$ and we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2{k}^{2}+6k & =0 \\\\ k(-2k+6) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $k=0$ and $k=3.$"}]}
